<p>Commentary is a reaction, which takes two pictures: the subject in a window — a browser row on top, tilted three degrees, lifted by a shadow — and the person beside it. The hand writes the reaction (“wait, what?”) and an arrow drawn in the accent points at the window. The title runs along the foot across both.</p>
